🤖 Multi-Agent Architecture
6 Specialized Agents
1. Curator Agent (Ingestion)

Parse documents (PDF, Markdown, DOCX)

Extract citations using GROBID or regex

Extract entities (concepts, methods, datasets)

Create graph nodes and relationships

Generate and store embeddings

2. Connector Agent (Relationships)

Find hidden connections via semantic similarity

Bibliographic coupling (papers citing same sources)

Graph path finding (indirect connections)

LLM-based relationship reasoning

Suggest new connections

3. Historian Agent (Evolution)

Track concept version changes

Analyze evolution trajectories

Identify milestone moments

Predict future directions

Generate evolution reports

4. Scout Agent (Trends)

Monitor arXiv, Semantic Scholar for new papers

Calculate citation velocity

Detect emerging concepts in my field

Identify research gaps

Alert on relevant new work

5. Composer Agent (Synthesis)

Generate Related Work sections

Create research questions

Synthesize literature reviews

Draft paper outlines

Generate abstracts with proper citations

6. Advisor Agent (Decisions)

Analyze concept maturity

Recommend validation experiments

Identify publication opportunities

Suggest next research steps

Generate research roadmap

